SUMMARY:Diwali\, Festival of Lights
DESCRIPTION:Diwali is celebrated by many Hindus\, Jains\, Sikhs\, and some Buddhists\, with traditions that vary across communities. Often associated with light\, hope\, renewal\, and the triumph of good over evil\, the festival brings families and communities together. Learning about Diwali is one way to celebrate religious diversity and build understanding across cultures. \nLearn more here.
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/diwali-festival-of-lights/
LOCATION:CA
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/Diwali.png
END:VEVENT
